<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-May 10.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-May 10.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended May 10:</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   305	   0.53     509500  155.40    9.06</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    215	   0.36     193950   41.70    8.73</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    370	   9.42     100800   37.30   33.19</p>
<p>ACC		   1270	   2.14	26720   33.93    8.79</p>
<p>IPCL		   138	   0.23     216500   29.88    8.69</p>
<p>Sterlite	     270	   0.45     103200   27.86    8.69</p>
<p>Castrol		425	   0.72	65150   27.69    8.83</p>
<p>MTNL		   290	   0.49	88300   25.61    8.81</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   835	   1.31	29500   24.63    8.18</p>
<p>Century Textiles  1830	   3.07	10520   19.25    8.75</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 10.03 percent on an annualised basis against 14.43 % in the previous carry forward account ended May 3</p>
